#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267512 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed361dfa-6b16-5d9d-b7cb-81007146a4bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267514} {:answer/id #uuid "78c3f94c-c4a9-5bf9-80f4-462cd2099cda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{36}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267515} {:answer/id #uuid "236f14d7-96f1-5754-ada4-0b63acc9f922" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267516} {:answer/id #uuid "18dbd1de-338c-50e0-a5b2-c658362e911e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267517} {:answer/id #uuid "e92be744-a538-5e8e-8575-cf982b7165c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267518}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18dbd1de-338c-50e0-a5b2-c658362e911e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267517} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4f66672-6bc0-5b5e-bf3b-cd857be4351f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267513}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "88a83a53-4b54-5fb6-8023-0cc5bd988bf8" :question/math-academy-id "q-115297" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072906/assets/1006eabe3321beb48df2cd936ff2252b77e8ded81f9c5b7aec4d143e43941088.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-4,0),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=6.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-4))^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-0)^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377532 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2073f727-f605-5e91-b847-f9e19272624c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377534} {:answer/id #uuid "2de53df5-06e4-5121-a129-ed3672717e72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{5}$ and $2\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377535} {:answer/id #uuid "1cb69cb6-49d7-5625-9f20-c7276b5be964" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377536} {:answer/id #uuid "f914e198-512f-5d0f-bab9-e5653ba8e114" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{5}$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377537} {:answer/id #uuid "6be03a1c-4ab8-5873-be88-bc55894420a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2de53df5-06e4-5121-a129-ed3672717e72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{5}$ and $2\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377535} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d149ec3-1bda-5a45-85df-69addf9bf489" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377533}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9ff8c2aa-59f0-5520-88ff-40444c85393f" :question/math-academy-id "q-16548" :question/problem "For the ellipse \n$\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{5}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{2}=1$, find the lengths of its major and minor axes." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=-4$ and $k=3,$ so the center is located at $(-4,3).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=5$ and ${b}^{2}=2.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=5,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{5}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=2,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=\\sqrt{5},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{5}=2\\sqrt{5},$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{2}=2\\sqrt{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275495 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "feeec65c-f199-549e-808b-af504a539680" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275497} {:answer/id #uuid "04d7531a-3dd9-52fd-985a-3fd86ed94c0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{6}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{8}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275498} {:answer/id #uuid "098b131c-f332-585a-ac9c-fc691451a7b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275499} {:answer/id #uuid "ee51484c-a6a4-5f40-ac70-b492972d1b91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{6}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275500} {:answer/id #uuid "b7eb24a9-f854-5eb4-b75c-5d018fc4d870" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7eb24a9-f854-5eb4-b75c-5d018fc4d870" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{16}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275501} :answer-field/id #uuid "3753699b-067a-5d56-8d77-f4bf7a64563d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275496}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "185f98a1-a00c-5fde-987b-3fdb1c0ac8f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-72252" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072906/assets/28079ead5ebb4649900653172d11c25f3ff489c6b34772094a1ba947c18ef3e1.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-2,-2),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=3,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-2))^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377539 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c9322e3-fa15-58f9-91b5-c1cddc94ba52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377541} {:answer/id #uuid "0ceb9980-8f25-5832-84de-7846ff273a0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377542} {:answer/id #uuid "dd7f343f-8451-5959-9146-f8465ca7dc54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377543} {:answer/id #uuid "542b3956-0f31-52fd-af8f-1aa6c1db9b23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377544} {:answer/id #uuid "30da9b57-bb55-5d5f-8ef1-debcc8c67c82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c9322e3-fa15-58f9-91b5-c1cddc94ba52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377541} :answer-field/id #uuid "67207b21-681e-5a03-98a1-1ea3e64f72eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377540}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4e456c69-2ce3-580a-a407-5f219437957a" :question/math-academy-id "q-7611" :question/problem "What is the center of the ellipse  $\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=3$ and $k=2,$ so the center is located at $(3,2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186267581 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62f3db3d-5735-5faf-81bf-cefe24de88fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267583} {:answer/id #uuid "43bd5ea6-0301-56e9-8c7c-a1b548a2ae67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{9}+(y+2)^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267584} {:answer/id #uuid "9add08b1-8336-57b1-9572-81bf40396815" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{3}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267585} {:answer/id #uuid "b647881b-35ee-58f9-8155-a91a17254dd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{3}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267586} {:answer/id #uuid "28ca37b7-8d58-5047-bcf6-c186bfa39cb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{9}+(y-2)^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267587}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62f3db3d-5735-5faf-81bf-cefe24de88fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267583} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8a692aa-2030-5107-8cc8-712b2f49e58d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267582}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fe64cee3-670f-56ea-b466-db8bdf57c963" :question/math-academy-id "q-7619" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072906/assets/2bc4b82c6cfae63026f221dd49cdc74a9ce3884443e933cae02c36f6d732707e.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-2,4),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=1,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-2))^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ (x+2)^{2}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
